{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/796971-when-frenzy-might-occur-in-combat","id":796971,"title":"When Frenzy might occur in Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T12:50:21-08:00","id":796971,"title":"When Frenzy might occur in Combat","content":"Something I was just thinking about. Frenzy should occur when dramatically appropriate, and we're given a list of sample triggers as possible ideas, along with the dice modifiers for resisting that Frenzy. So thinking about how combat actually goes, one of the suggested ones is &quot;Wounded (at all)&quot; which makes sense! You get hit, the vampire equivalent of flight or fight (Frenzy) kicks in and all that. <br /> <br /> The question I have is what kinds of vampires would you make roll for that? If all of them do, it's a ticking time-bomb situation, but I could imagine older vampires or those who frequently engage in violence might not trigger frenzy in this situation. What do you think?<br /> <br /> What about when you draw blood from an enemy? Would you qualify that as &quot;Seeing a trivial open wound&quot; or as something else? One obvious situation for a Vampire to frenzy in this case is when they're already Hungry or Starving. When else do you think you'd ask for the check?<br /> <br /> I'm aware of the answers provided by the book, but I'd love to hear people's thoughts or play experiences, since in the game I've been playing we've been sort of under-served by Frenzy and I've noted it to my ST. I play a character who isn't a combatant by nature or habit, so I imagine they'd often frenzy in life-threatening situations for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T13:04:24-08:00","id":796986,"title":"","content":"I like to call for a Frenzy roll when a vampire would otherwise be Beaten Down (i.e. when they take bashing &gt; stamina or any amount of lethal). Any less than that I don't really consider a serious enough injury to be a dramatically appropriate moment to risk frenzy, unless the player takes the initiative and says their character would risk frenzy in this situation.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a Beaten Down opponent is a dramatically interesting trigger for a Frenzy check (<i>especially</i> if they're surrendering), but a character that's been smacked for a point or two of bashing isn't to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:31:33-08:00","id":797088,"title":"","content":"Using that Beaten Down metric is fantastic and something I hadn't thought about, thanks for that.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it now, the bit about any time Kindred take lethal damage particularly makes a lot of sense. Rollover means you've taken quite the beating, and supernatural or highly lethal sources of damage that still do lethal seem like natural triggers for the Beast.<br /> <br /> Here's a question: How often do players in your games volunteer the suggestion that their character will Frenzy? Do you feel it's appropriate to follow that, or do you prefer that the ST remain in charge of that?<br /> <br /> I've been in situations where I felt my character would frenzy, but I also have Blood Potency 2, so it offers me an advantage in combat when she does frenzy. Despite thinking it's appropriate, I do feel a little skeevy when I personally think my character might Frenzy, because I don't want to come off as dice-grubbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:41:22-08:00","id":797092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/796971-when-frenzy-might-occur-in-combat?p=797088#post797088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using that Beaten Down metric is fantastic and something I hadn't thought about, thanks for that.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it now, the bit about any time Kindred take lethal damage particularly makes a lot of sense. Rollover means you've taken quite the beating, and supernatural or highly lethal sources of damage that still do lethal seem like natural triggers for the Beast.<br /> <br /> Here's a question: How often do players in your games volunteer the suggestion that their character will Frenzy? Do you feel it's appropriate to follow that, or do you prefer that the ST remain in charge of that?<br /> <br /> I've been in situations where I felt my character would frenzy, but I also have Blood Potency 2, so it offers me an advantage in combat when she does frenzy. Despite thinking it's appropriate, I do feel a little skeevy when I personally think my character might Frenzy, because I don't want to come off as dice-grubbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players very rarely volunteer for a Frenzy check. If they want it for the extra dice on physical pools, they'll try to ride the wave, but the loss of control involved in a regular Frenzy (even though I allow them to maintain control their characters, they're just restricted in their roleplaying) is enough of a deterrent that they usually don't want it to happen if it doesn't have to. The occasional exceptions are actually usually out of combat, and have more to do with things personal to the character. When it does happen I'm happy to go along with it. Even if I got the impression that a player was doing it for the bonus dice, I'd probably be alright with it, unless it seemed wildly out of character. Though, I can't recall that ever happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-30-2015, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T22:48:42-08:00","id":797206,"title":"","content":"<br /> My vampire tended to frenzy when she got into combat against other vampires, it usually came up immediately after lashing out (when it often failed). In the combat situations I asked for her to frenzy, and it was a part of her tactic. The ST ruled that she couldn't do anything terribly sophisticated during a frenzy, but I maintained control of her actions. <br /> <br /> She also frenzied upon learning her brother had been staked and destroyed, that was a call by the ST. He was one of her touchstones, though by the time he was staked her humanity was too low to have him as a touchstone. <br /> <br /> There were also a couple of times when the ST asked if my character would frenzy in the situation. <br /> <br /> Another time, an NPC vampire frenzied during combat when he encountered a bane. <br /> <br /> Looking back, frenzy added a lot of interesting aspects to the play. Socially, it was always a bit embarrassing to &quot;lose it&quot;, especially when everyone else stayed under control In combat it gives you that feel of monstrous power fitting for a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:34:48-08:00","id":797261,"title":"","content":"I call for frenzy every time in combat. Combat is a tense situation, adrenaline running high, instinct and that flight/fight responce kicking in. That's what the angry beast is all about. Keeping your mind clear (or riding the wave) is difficult manner. <br /> <br /> There's a reason why vampires play at being friendly and social. Because, when it comes to violence, nothing stops them from destroying each other. Yes, this makes vampires ticking time bombs. That's the theme I like to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}